-- MT-CN: Chinese labels for the Wearable Devices configuration UI (the Alt+M window).
--
-- WHY A SCRIPT AND NOT A TEXT FILE: the pack translates by string id through
-- gamedata/configs/text/chs/*.xml, and WD's own table is complete (eng and chs both carry 53 ids,
-- zero diff; every ui_mcm_wd_*/st_wd_* id the scripts reference exists in chs). The English you see
-- in this UI is different in kind - about 133 strings are hardcoded Lua literals (`label = "Anim
-- Speed"`, row labels like "Yaw (Y)"), not ids, so no XML file can ever reach them. Editing the pack
-- is off limits, so the labels are rewritten at the one moment they are still data: WD registers its
-- tabs/devices through wd_gui, which happens inside wd_boot's on_game_start, i.e. after every script
-- file has loaded. Wrapping those entry points from this zzz_-named file therefore runs before any
-- registration, and needs no pack file touched.
--
-- Term choices follow the pack's own Chinese, not new coinages: factions come from
-- st_rigged_community_* (强盗/晴空/纪律团/自由团/雇佣兵/军方/科学家/黑石/罪孽/变节者/自由潜行者),
-- "你的阵营" from ui_mcm_lst_idiots_faction, 护腕/手表/荧光棒/精神/耐力/辐射/状态 from the pack's
-- existing usage, except the two device names, which follow the user's chosen terms (Promin ->
-- 护腕PDA, Vektor -> 护腕表) rather than the pack's own Latin item names (st_promin = Promin,
-- st_vektor_name = Vektor): the UI reads better with them, and the item still shows Promin in the
-- inventory. ISG stays as-is.
--
-- Matching is exact on the whole string, never substring, so ambiguous words ("Map", "Scale",
-- "Time", "Range") cannot bleed into unrelated text; anything absent from MAP is left untouched,
-- which is also what happens if the pack later renames a label. No id-like key can be caught here,
-- because every key contains a space or is a capitalized word, and translation ids are snake_case.
--
-- Engine Lua printf substitutes %s only.
if not wd_gui then
    printf("[MT-CN] wd i18n skipped: wd_gui not loaded yet")
    return
end

